# Container services stubbed out on the mindphone (codename "mindset").
#
# Android's battery health HAL. Nothing in LuneOS consumes it: batteryd and
# nyx read the battery straight from sysfs, and LuneOS's own storaged is a
# different daemon living outside the container. What it does cost is sleep.
# Traced on the phone 2026-09-21 with the alarm tracepoints that the debugfs
# fix made available:
#
#   health@2.1-serv alarmtimer_start ... type:BOOTTIME  interval 600 s
#   health@2.1-serv alarmtimer_start ... type:BOOTTIME  interval  60 s
#
# A BOOTTIME alarm wakes the SoC, so this polled the battery every ten
# minutes from suspend, and every sleep in the preceding measurements ended
# at 590-599 s on the PMIC. The same HAL is stubbed on the Google targets for
# the same reason.
vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.health@2.1-service
# ... and Android's storaged with it, which is the HAL's only consumer inside
# the container. It must go in the same breath: with the HAL stubbed and
# storaged left running, storaged asks hwservicemanager for
# android.hardware.health@2.0::IHealth/default once a second and init logs a
# failed ctl.interface_start for each one. Measured on the phone the first
# time the HAL was stubbed alone - one such line in the whole preceding boot,
# then a steady 60 a minute from the moment the stub took effect. sargo pairs
# these two for exactly this reason. LuneOS's own storaged is a different
# daemon outside the container and is untouched by this.
system/bin/storaged
# Android's USB-OTG storage FUSE daemon (service fuse_usbotg runs
# /system/bin/sdcard for /storage/usbotg). Nothing mounts OTG media into the
# container under LuneOS, so it exits immediately and init restarts it every
# five seconds for the life of the boot - measured here at 12 starts a minute
# sustained across a two-hour boot, each one dragging in a
# flags_health_check exec and an "exited 4 times before boot completed"
# complaint. Same daemon, same treatment as the MP01.
system/bin/sdcard
# The combo-chip firmware dump collector (service stp_dump in init_connectivity.rc runs
# /vendor/bin/stp_dump3). The vendor build.prop ships persist.vendor.connsys.coredump.mode=2, a debug
# setting that starts it, and with nothing to hand a dump to it busy-loops on pselect6() for /dev/stpwmt
# without ever reading it: about 4,700 calls a second, 54,249 s of CPU time in a 54,653 s uptime
# (2026-10-06), a whole core for the life of the boot. Diagnostics only; nothing in LuneOS consumes them.
# Same treatment as the MP01.
vendor/bin/stp_dump3
